(1) ApiSignInRoleList
- This program is to show internal (I) or external (E) user type in a list.....dropdown list?
- Allowing end-user to choose more specific - Sign-In or using Email in case user forgot their sign-In or email
- We cater the search in wildcard ...left and right

//Request type is Setup for sign in save
###
POST {{baseUrl}}/sp/ApiSignInRoleList/queryasync HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authorization}}
content-type: application/json

{
  "UserType": "E",
  "SignIn" : "",
  "Email":""
}

(2) ApiSignInRole
- Double click on the list ...Return to backend with @SignIn, @UsrId, @UserType and @EttyId
- The @EttyId must be > 0 if it is an existing CustEttyId otherwise it should be is NULL
- On screen:
>>> Provide dropdown list to show CustEttyId
>>> Provide dropdown list to show UserSts (VwLibRef where RefType = 'USERSTS'
>>> Provide dropdown list to show UserRole (VwLibRef where RefType = 'USERROLE'
>>> Provide dropdown list to show AccessSts (VwLibRef where RefType = 'USERSTS'     

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/sp/ApiSignInRole/queryasync HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authorization}}
content-type: application/json

{
  "UsrId": 53,
  "EttyId":1424,
  "UserType": "E",
  "SignIn": "ali002",
}

(3) ApiSignInRoleSave
Call program
EXEC dbo.ApiSignInRoleSave
	@SignIn		,
	@UsrId		,
	@UserType	,
	@EttyId		,
	@WebEttyUId	 OUTPUT,
	@UserRole	,
	@AccessSts	,
	@MobileNo	,
	@Email		,
	@UserId		,
	@SrcIpAddr	,
	@MsgId		 OUTPUT

UserSts is the Sign-In status.......AccessSts is the level of CustEttyId access status

